[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_impl_pretense.py: Defect confirmed against low/ring_buffer_impl.pyi and low/ring_buffer.pyi: the push override (lines 43-59) and pop override (lines 61-75) are not contract-faithful because they both call_target the SUT AND mutate self.state.items (push pops the oldest item when saturated then appends the new item; pop discards items[0]), duplicating the model bookkeeping already performed by the inherited interface transition, which delegates into these overrides through inner_transition under the checked adapter. Net effect: each push/pop mutates the model twice, so after pushes to capacity and repeated pops the model size drifts from the real deque and size (line 106, must satisfy the contracted 'current number of items stored' postcondition) and snapshot_items (line 90, must satisfy the contracted 'all stored items in FIFO arrival order, non-destructive' postcondition) fail, and the size-decrements-by-exactly-one postcondition is violated (observed size drops by two). The author's CHANGE added call_target pivots and model-state asserts but did not remove the duplicate model mutation, so the postconditions still fail. Required fix: overrides must not mutate self.state.items; only call_target the SUT and assert the contracted return/postcondition against model state captured before delegation, leaving model bookkeeping to the inherited interface transition. Reproduce with the failing real test sequence push alpha, push beta, push gamma, pop, pop, then observe size/is_empty, and the property fuzz sequence push, push, size.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_impl_pretense.py: Remove duplicate model bookkeeping from RingBufferImplPseudoStateMachine overrides: push/pop/clear no longer mutate self.state.items, so each checked call performs model bookkeeping exactly once (in the inherited interface transition that delegates through inner_transition). Overrides now only call_target the SUT and assert contracted returns/postconditions against model state captured before delegation (push evicted-vs-None, pop oldest item, clear void return, snapshot FIFO copy, capacity/size/is_empty/is_full observations). This fixes the reported size drift (size dropping by two) and restores the size/snapshot_items postconditions.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_pretense.py: Reorder RingBufferStateMachine.push so all model bookkeeping happens after the inner_transition pivot: was_full/oldest/evicted are computed non-destructively before the pivot, and the eviction pop plus append occur afterwards. This keeps model pre-state pristine at the pivot so a delegating implementation override observes the true pre-call state (e.g. push to a full buffer correctly expects the oldest item as the evicted return), without changing fake transition semantics.
